WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:09.160
People often ask me just how dire I think
the state of free speech in America.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.110
In the last two weeks I've spoken at several
college campuses in California, Arizona, and

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:19.599
Texas, as well as attended a conference in
Dallas primarily focused on free speech from

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:21.680
an academic perspective.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:29.460
I spoke to dozens of professors who feel the
ability to truly exchange ideas or express

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.949
unpopular opinions on their campus is at uniquely
perilous cross roads.

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:39.140
The university of Berkley, once the home for
the free speech movement in this country,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.550
quite literally went up in flames when Milo
spoke there.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.260
People with fairly moderate opinions like
professor Jordan Petersen and historian Charles

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:54.920
Murray are shouted down by self righteous
students on college campuses.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.309
Ann Coulter was first barred by Berkely, and
then told she could only speak on a day when

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:02.930
students weren't having classes on campus.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:08.670
These safe spaces and trigger warnings...concepts
designed to protect feelings instead of dealing

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.869
with facts...coupled with constant smearing
of any intellectual opponents as racists or

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:20.499
bigots, has birthed a generation who are increasingly
intolerant of tolerance.

00:01:20.499 --> 00:01:26.340
I should also be clear here -- it really is
one side who's being far more intolerant on

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.649
campuses today.

00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:33.630
Just think, if any college campus invited
a far Left Marxist or Communist who wanted

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:38.679
to end capitalism and ultimately destroy the
United States, there would be virtually no

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:39.679
outcry.

00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:44.180
The Marxists and Communists would have their
event, with maybe a few curious people challenging

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.179
their ideas during a Q&amp;A, and that would be
it.

00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:51.869
The absolute reverse is happening all over
the country when a conservative -- or any

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:55.619
non-Leftist speakers -- are invited to college
campuses.

00:01:55.619 --> 00:02:03.619
Ben Shapiro has been banned from DePaul for
sharing his brand of mainstream conservative

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:04.859
thought.

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:10.640
Antifa, the self proclaimed anti facists,
who actually use facist tactics to silence

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:16.050
their opponents, and who dress like Cobra
soldiers from GI Joe, issued a statement and

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:21.420
threatened to protest Portland State when
Christina Hoff Sommers, Peter Boghhosian and

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.969
I spoke there.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:27.519
Apparently they found something more anti
LGBTQ and anti women right before we started,

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:29.450
so they moved their protests elsewhere.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:36.980
And of course, as I always say and will continue
to say, you have every right to protest and

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.900
use your speech to counter someone else's
speech.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.540
What you don't have a right to do is silence
someone else by using violence or intimidation.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:53.109
This is why I talk so much about self-censorship
and chill effect around free speech.

00:02:53.109 --> 00:02:58.000
Violence not only silences the speakers of
today, but in essence it silences the speakers

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.329
of tomorrow who will quiet themselves instead
of dealing with the protests and smears and

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:08.670
everything else that comes with being someone
outside of group think.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.359
What's being stolen from these college students
is the ability to learn how to think about

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:18.560
complex issues while in university, so they
can be equipped to engage with diverse set

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.760
of ideas in the real real world.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:26.579
And that diversity, diversity of thought is
far more important that diversity of immutable

00:03:26.579 --> 00:03:30.709
characteristics be it race relgion or sexuality.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.530
Last week I spoke at University of Arizona
with my friend and former guest Michael Shermer.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.840
It turned out that there was a trans holocaust
denier in the crowd.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.540
Yes, trans holocaust deniers do exist.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:49.659
Not only did we not silence her, but we opened
up the floor for her to ask us questions.

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:57.599
Michael, the editor in Chief of Skeptic magazine,
who specializes in debunking conspiracy theories,

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:04.430
an expert in debunking holocaust denial myths,
answered her questions clearly and with facts.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.159
The students in the room didn't attack her
or kick her out despite her abhorrent beliefs.

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:14.620
It was a truly beautiful moment which shows
why free speech is so important.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.970
We exercised our right to talk openly at a
public event in which anyone was welcome to

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:24.800
join, as she shared her ideas, which we countered
with better ideas.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:30.300
While I suspect Michael didn't change her
mind on holocaust denial, we put our principles

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.970
of free expression to the test.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:38.620
This open discussion with a wide array of
opinion is how you expand knowledge and figure

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:45.250
out what you believe, NOT by silencing, shaming,
and defaming your ideological opponent.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:52.750
Sadly, the true tolerance that we experienced
in that room is a rarity on college these

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.750
days.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.139
I know I don't have to sell you guys on the
lunacy that's happening at college campuses.

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:01.130
You see it everyday with the language police
telling people what pronouns to use, or else!,

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:06.720
and the endless stream of insane stories coming
from America's campuses showing how intolerant

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.580
the so called "tolerant side" has become.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:14.460
What I would like to focus on here, is the
creeping groupthink an obfuscation around

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:20.050
free thought free speech that is no creeping
up into the political echelon.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:25.030
Just this week you may have seen new Democratic
National Committee chairman Tom Perez say

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.210
the DNC won't back any politicians who aren't
pro-choice.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:34.990
While I have no problem with the party having
a set of beliefs as a guideline for its policies,

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:41.050
this type of intolerance to other ideas, even
if they're incredibly difficult topics like

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:47.470
abortion, set a terrible precedent for the
exchange of ideas in a pluralistic society.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:51.970
This specific event isn't a direct threat
to free speech, but it does go to the heart

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:58.879
of how intolerance by the Left is driving
otherwise liberal people, to the center.

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:04.000
Or, as the Left calls it, the neo nazi alt
right white suprmacist far right.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.020
The more egregious assault on free speech
in the last few days though was from former

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:13.629
head of the DNC and former Presidential candidate
Howard Dean.

00:06:13.629 --> 00:06:20.379
Dean is a progressive who at this point really
sums up why this ideology is not truly for

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:25.250
progression of freedom and liberalism, but
for regression of them.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:29.889
After hearing that Ann Coulter was going to
be banned from Berkely, Dean claimed that

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.610
Coulter's hate speech was not protected by
the first amendment.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:32.610
IMAGE: https://twitter.com/RubinReport/status/855450593715945473

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.340
"Ann Coulter's Hate Speech is not protected
by the first Amendment."

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:37.509
Well actually Howard, it is.

00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:38.509
100%.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:39.509
Absolutely.

00:06:39.509 --> 00:06:45.150
Full stop.First off, he uses the amorphous
term 'hate speech' sounds like something but

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.759
doesn't actually exist.

00:06:46.759 --> 00:06:51.850
Yes, you can't call for direct violence to
a person or a group, that's a criminal offense,

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:55.190
but you are allowed to say hateful and mean
things.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.530
That's the very part of free speech that we
have to protect because the definition of

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:04.680
hate speech will just keep expanding until
it includes any speech that the veers ever

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.280
so slightly away from group think.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:12.450
Beyond Dean's confusion about hate speech,
he also apparently doesn't know what the first

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.750
Amendment is.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:18.740
As I know you know, the first Amendment is
about prohibiting the government from making

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:24.520
any laws prohibiting free speech, it has absolutely
nothing to do with the speech of a private

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.669
person, or hate speech, or a university deplatforming
a speaker.

00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:36.639
If you truly care about minorities, college
Republicans ARE a minority in most universities,

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:42.680
and they deserve to be heard from, just like
anyone else who has been offered a platform.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:47.860
Sadly, Dean is a progressive thought leader
while he seemingly has no idea about the very

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.229
constitution our political leaders are supposed
to defend.

00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:57.610
With this is mind, I still absolutely believe
the best way to beat the violent tactics of

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:02.879
Antifa or the intellectually challenged ideas
of Howard Dean, is to counter them with better

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:04.000
ideas.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.719
We shouldn't stoop to their level of violence,
or try to take away their free speech.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:13.039
We should teach the ideas of liberty, freedom,
and true liberalism.

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:18.139
Yes, they'll always scream louder than us,
or act out more hysterically, but I believe

00:08:18.139 --> 00:08:24.289
our game is a long one and our better ideas
will win if we actually put them into practice.

00:08:24.289 --> 00:08:30.780
With this in mind, we're continuing our partnership
with Learn Liberty this week with Brandon

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:35.100
Turner, a professor of political science and
George Mason University.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:40.120
He's an expert in political theory, with extensive
knowledge of the writings of everyone from

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.590
John Stuart Mill to Karl Marx.

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:47.580
We're going to explore political thinkers
from all across the map to see which ideas

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.860
stand the test of time.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.370
Right or left, democrat or Republican, male
or female, gay or straight, every single issue

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:58.640
starts with our ability to discuss it and
figure out what we believe.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:04.740
If we can unite against the forces that will
silence us we may find allies in places we

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.090
never thought we would.

